# .gitignore — Backend

# ╔═ Environment & Secrets ════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ NEVER commit these. They contain API keys, database passwords, and        ║
# ║ other sensitive configuration that changes per machine.                   ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Instead:                                                                   ║
# ║  1. Create .env locally (not in git)                                      ║
# ║  2. Share a .env.example with placeholder values (GROQ_API_KEY=xxx)       ║
# ║  3. Team members copy .env.example → .env and fill in their own keys      ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production


# ╔═ Python Virtual Environment ═══════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ The venv/ folder contains Python packages specific to your project.       ║
# ║ Size: 100MB+ (don't commit!)                                              ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ When teammates clone the project, they run:                               ║
# ║   python3 -m venv venv                                                    ║
# ║   source venv/bin/activate  (or venv\Scripts\activate on Windows)         ║
# ║   pip install -r requirements.txt                                          ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ This recreates the venv on their machine with the same package versions.  ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv
.venv/
.env_venv/


# ╔═ Python Cache & Compiled Files ════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ __pycache__: Generated when Python imports .py files                      ║
# ║ *.pyc:       Compiled Python bytecode (machine-specific)                  ║
# ║ *.pyo:       Optimized Python bytecode                                    ║
# ║ *.pyd:       Python extension module                                      ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ These are auto-generated and useless in a repo.                           ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python


# ╔═ IDEs & Editors ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ VS Code, PyCharm, Sublime, vim, etc. each create their own config files.  ║
# ║ These are personal — your teammate's editor setup shouldn't end up in     ║
# ║ the shared repo.                                                          ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Teams usually share a .editorconfig or CONTRIBUTING.md instead, which     ║
# ║ explains the linting rules (line length, indentation) without requiring   ║
# ║ everyone to commit their own .vscode/settings.json.                       ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.sublime-workspace


# ╔═ Testing & Coverage ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Pytest and coverage tools generate reports that are local to your machine ║
# ║ and should be regenerated fresh each time.                                ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions, etc.) generate their own coverage data  ║
# ║ and upload it to services like Codecov.                                   ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.hypothesis/


# ╔═ Build & Distribution ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ If you ever package your backend as a Python package (e.g. with setuptools),
# ║ these folders are auto-generated during build and should never be committed.
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ For a simple API project, you won't hit these, but it's good practice to ║
# ║ include them.                                                             ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg


# ╔═ Database Files ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ If you ever add SQLite (or other file-based databases), don't commit the  ║
# ║ .db files. They contain user data and vary per environment.               ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ For this project, we're using JSON, so you can comment these out.         ║
# ║ Keep them for future reference.                                           ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.DatabaseCredentials


# ╔═ Logs & Temp Files ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Application logs and temporary files are ephemeral — they should never    ║
# ║ end up in version control.                                                ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp


# ╔═ OS-Specific Files ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ macOS and Windows create these automatically. They clutter commits and    ║
# ║ cause merge conflicts across platforms.                                   ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db


# ╔═ Linting & Formatting Tools ══════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Black, isort, flake8, etc. sometimes generate cache files.                ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.black/


# ╔═ Environment-Specific Configs ════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ If you use uvicorn directly (not Docker), you might create a .env file   ║
# ║ specific to development, testing, or production. All should be ignored.  ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

.env.dev
.env.test
.env.staging


# ╔═ Optional: Commit These Instead ══════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Instead of ignoring these forever, create versions WITH placeholder      ║
# ║ values that you DO commit. Team members use them as templates.            ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ║ Examples:                                                                 ║
# ║   .env.example       ← GROQ_API_KEY=paste_your_key_here                  ║
# ║   requirements.txt   ← should be committed (lists all dependencies)       ║
# ║   pyproject.toml     ← should be committed (if using Poetry)              ║
# ║                                                                            ║
# ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝